  "tokens": [
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A row is an ordering of pitch classes, and a pitch class is not a spelling." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Open Music Theory's `108-basics-of-twelve-tone-theory.md` asks for a row —" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// each pitch class once, in an order — before it asks for anything else, and" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `109-naming-conventions-for-rows.md` names the four things that can be done" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// to one: prime, inversion, retrograde, and retrograde inversion. This file" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// builds a row, shows what makes a list of numbers fail to be one, and applies" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// each of those four as a single operation." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Every value below has forgotten which letter a note was written with. The" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// only way back into notation is `row_spelled_in`, which takes the collection" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// that decides the spelling and answers nothing where that collection has no" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// such note." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// **Where this stops.** `110-row-properties.md` counts the labelled forms — the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// 4n of them, the matrix, and the operations that fix a row — and those cost" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// more reduction steps than `02-core-calculus.md` §4's budget allows today." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `row_forms`, `distinct_forms`, `row_symmetries`, and `matrix` are in" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `std::post_tonal::serial` and are prompt 165's to exercise. What is here is" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// what one operation costs." },
    { "kind": "piece", "text": "piece" },
    { "kind": "string", "text": "\"Serial Forms\"" },
